' purpose: Approved development preparation reports setup completion separately from F9 readiness.
' covers: mise.toml
' covers: rust-toolchain.toml
' covers: package.json
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/prepare.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/acquire-tools.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/tests/acquire-tools.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/check-bundle.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/stages.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/snapshots.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/create.sh
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/seed.sh
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/install-rust.sh
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/tests/preparation.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/tests/stages.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/tests/snapshots.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/tests/setup.test.mjs
' covers: tooling/sbx-dev/README.md
' related: _spec/tooling/bun-first-party-tooling.puml
' related: _spec/tooling/native-ingress/f9-diagnostic.puml
' invariant: No automatic retry, resume, reset, rollback or removal.
' rationale: [HIGH] Checking mutable host paths before copying does not bind the bytes a provider later reads.
' contract: The fixed guest wrapper receives installer path/SHA, archive SHA and attempt only as positional arguments.
' note-register: P right preview FK 11.5; P/C approval FK 10.7; A right scope FK 10.4.
' note-register: A/STATE intent FK 11.6; A/B provenance FK 12.0; C/STATE recovery FK 11.5.
' note-register: C/VM policy FK 11.4; P/VM diagnosis FK 12.9.
' note-register: S right host binding FK 12.2; VM right installer binding FK 12.2; S/VM limits FK 11.2.
' FK syllables: hand-counted English; executables=5, mise=1, sysroot=2, CLI=3, F9=2, KUnit=3.
' FK syllables: UID=3; read-only and in-place each count as two words.
@startuml sbx-preparation
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Development setup: automatic host inputs, separate guest approvals
actor Executor as OP
participant "prepare.mjs\ndev:sbx:prepare parent" as P <<app>>
participant "acquire-tools.mjs\ndev:sbx:acquire child" as A <<app>>
participant "check-bundle.mjs" as B <<app>>
participant "stages.mjs\nseven sequential mise children" as C <<app>>
participant "snapshots.mjs\nbounded Bun worker" as S <<app>>
participant "Named development sbx" as VM <<host>>
participant "mise\ncore backends on host" as TOOLS <<host>>
database "Private 0700 run directory\n0600 acquisition / state / policy / report\n0400 complete provision snapshots" as STATE <<db>>

OP -> TOOLS : review mise.toml; explicitly mise trust
OP -> TOOLS : mise install (online host bootstrap)
TOOLS --> OP : core:bun@1.4.0 + core:rust@1.95.0
note over OP, TOOLS
  mise.toml: exact built-in backend pins
  Rust matches rust-toolchain.toml
  auto_install=false
end note

OP -> P : --plan: syntax and task graph only
P -> P : toolPins(): read checked-in configuration
P --> OP : no children, executable resolution, directories or network
note right of P
  Preview reads configured pins but runs no
  children, creates no files and resolves no
  executables. Explicit host bootstrap supplies
  Bun before preview, since mise has disabled
  its own automatic installation.
end note

OP -> P : mise run dev:sbx:prepare (no input flags)
P -> P : require stdin TTY; resolve mise and sbx from current PATH
note over P, C
  Parent entry precheck: stdin TTY
  Acquisition/stage approval: stdin AND stderr TTY
end note
P -> STATE : allocate fresh run directory
alt default: no bundle or digest supplied
  P -> A : mise run --raw dev:sbx:acquire -- --manifest <private-run>/tools.json
  A -> A : acquireTools(): require Linux x64; read exact matching configured pins
  A -> OP : fresh terminal approval: host downloads + bounded packaging
  A -> STATE : exclusively record rust-tools.tar.intent
  note over A, STATE
    Record private intent before host installs
    and publish the manifest only after
    validation. Keep partial artifacts when
    acquisition fails, since a retry cannot prove
    whether shared toolchain storage changed.
  end note
  A -> TOOLS : install --jobs 1 core:rust@1.95.0
  A -> TOOLS : exec core:rust@1.95.0 -- rustc -vV
  A -> TOOLS : exec core:rust@1.95.0 -- rustc --print sysroot
  A -> TOOLS : exec core:rust@1.95.0 -- cargo --version
  TOOLS --> A : checked Rust/Cargo 1.95.0; x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
  note over A, TOOLS
    Install: <=600s, output <=64KiB
    Discovery: 3 x <=30s, output <=16KiB each
    Pack/hash/validation budget: 120s
    Archive <=2GiB; expanded <=4GiB
    Members <=20,000; manifest <=8KiB
  end note
  note right of TOOLS
    Shared mise/rustup caches: no F9 quota
    Approval pauses: no automatic deadline
  end note
  A -> A : select actual sysroot: bin/rustc + bin/cargo + lib/**
  note right of A
    Selected sysroot paths exclude home
    directories, caches and credentials from
    the guest archive.
    Resolve internal links, but refuse cycles,
    special files and links escaping the sysroot.
  end note
  note over A, B
    Optional fixed regular notice leaves:
    LICENSE-APACHE, LICENSE-MIT, COPYRIGHT
    at the sysroot root or share/doc/rust/
    No recursive documentation copy
  end note
  A -> STATE : stream rust-tools.tar: regular files/directories, no links
  A -> A : compute SHA-256 within packaging budget
  A -> B : validate hash/layout; remaining budget; output <=16KiB\ngraceMilliseconds=1000
  note over A, B
    Validator supervisors: TERM grace 1000ms
    Then KILL + <=2s reap; refusal unchanged
    Leaf tar: grace 0; <=30s / <=8MiB
  end note
  B -> B : runBounded(/usr/bin/tar, explicit clean env)\nparse metadata only after bounded success
  B --> A : BUNDLE=HASH_AND_LAYOUT_OK
  A -> STATE : exclusively publish tools.json
  note right of STATE
    dev-sbx-acquired-tools-v1 (exact keys)
    schema, bunVersion, rustVersion, host,
    bundlePath, sha256
    bundlePath = <private-run>/rust-tools.tar
  end note
  P -> A : readAcquiredTools(<private-run>/tools.json): private manifest + bundle
  A --> P : automatic bundlePath + sha256
  note over A, B
    The manifest binds configured Bun and
    checked Rust/Cargo versions, host and archive
    integrity. It does not authenticate upstream
    sources or validate inherited mise settings
    and previously installed files.
  end note
else advanced offline: --bundle AND --sha256
  P -> P : skip acquisition; require absolute archive + lowercase digest
end

P -> C : mise run --raw dev:sbx:validate
C -> OP : approve local validation
C -> B : revalidate archive hash/layout: <=60s / output <=16KiB\ngraceMilliseconds=1000
C -> STATE : pin archive + fixed installer / attempt state
P -> C : mise run --raw dev:sbx:create-stage
C -> OP : approve one ls/create/ls attempt
C -> VM : create.sh: mountless; --pull never; --skills off\n--deny-network '**'; --cpus 2; --memory 4g
VM --> C : generated name + confirmed result
C -> STATE : carry name automatically
P -> C : mise run --raw dev:sbx:policy
C -> OP : approve private policy readback
C -> VM : policy ls --wide NAME
C -> STATE : bounded policy + digest
P -> C : mise run --raw dev:sbx:accept-policy
C -> OP : inspect file; accept this digest/name
group Snapshot provision and descriptor-bound installation
  P -> C : mise run --raw dev:sbx:provision
  C -> OP : approve local snapshots + two copies; stdin AND stderr TTY
  C -> STATE : persist inFlightStage='provision'; consume policy acknowledgement
  C -> S : host Bun --no-env-file --no-install snapshots.mjs --state STATE_PATH\n<=60s / combined output <=16KiB
  S -> STATE : read bound state; derive both attempt-specific snapshot paths
  note over S, STATE
    prefix = statePath + '.' + attemptId
    prefix + '.bundle.snapshot.tar'
    prefix + '.installer.snapshot.sh'
    dev-sbx-workflow-v1 remains unchanged
  end note
  S -> S : open approved bundle + fixed installer: O_NOFOLLOW, regular files
  S -> STATE : exclusive 0600 snapshots; bounded copy + approved SHA-256\nfstat unchanged; complete files become 0400
  note right of S
    Snapshot approved bytes before provider copy,
    since a mutable pathname can change after
    validation. Private read-only artifacts keep
    subsequent source replacement from changing
    the approved transfer inputs.
  end note
  note over S, STATE
    Bundle <=2GiB; fixed installer <=64KiB
    Extra retained disk <=2GiB +64KiB/attempt
    Partial snapshots remain after failure
    No overwrite, retry or automatic cleanup
  end note
  S --> C : SNAPSHOTS=VERIFIED_PRIVATE_INPUTS; both snapshots read-only
  C -> B : validate SNAPSHOT bundle hash/layout: <=60s / output <=16KiB\ngraceMilliseconds=1000
  C -> VM : cp bundle SNAPSHOT -> existing attempt guest archive\n<=90s / output <=16KiB
  C -> VM : cp installer SNAPSHOT -> existing attempt guest installer\n<=45s / output <=16KiB
  P -> C : mise run --raw dev:sbx:install
  C -> OP : approve bounded guest install; stdin AND stderr TTY
  C -> VM : existing timeout; fixed /bin/sh -c wrapper; positional path/SHA inputs\nhost <=130s / output <=16KiB; guest 120s + kill-after 2s
  VM -> VM : open guest installer once as fd 3
  VM -> VM : sha256sum checks approved installer SHA via /proc/self/fd/3
  VM -> VM : exec /bin/sh /proc/self/fd/3 with archive SHA + attempt\noffline Rust/Cargo 1.95.0 checks
  note right of VM
    Open the guest installer once and verify its
    approved digest through that descriptor.
    Execute the same descriptor so a pathname
    replacement after hashing cannot substitute
    different installer bytes.
  end note
  note over S, VM
    Read-only private snapshots narrow pathname
    races rather than defend against compromised
    same-UID processes.
    Guest descriptor binding also cannot prevent
    in-place writes to that same open inode.
  end note
end
P -> C : mise run --raw dev:sbx:diagnose
C -> OP : approve diagnostic scope
C -> C : invoke original f9-diagnose.mjs in host Bun\nrunBounded(..., graceMilliseconds=1000)
note over C, VM
  Outer deadline: 60s / output <=128KiB
  TERM helper group for cooperative CLI cleanup
  KILL after 1s; reap allowance <=2s
  Failure and interruption still refuse
end note
C -> VM : bounded listing, policy readback and guest shell capability probe
C -> STATE : accept original helper exit 2 only with matching complete STOP report
P -> P : composePreparation returns developmentPrepared=true; diagnosticComplete=true\nSTOP; f9Qualified=false; trainingReady=false

group Parent CLI presentation: main(argv)
  alt actual composePreparation returns its successful final receipt
    P --> OP : stdout: unchanged parent JSON first
    P --> OP : stderr: fixed DEVELOPMENT_SETUP_COMPLETE summary\nF9_NOT_ASSESSED; parent exit 2 is intentional\nhint: offline explainer presentation success 0 / rejected report 2; use receipt reportPath
  else --plan, failed preparation or non-terminal stdin
    P --> OP : no setup-completion text\nplan exits 0; refusal exits 2
  end
  note right of P
    No humanSummary or other JSON additions
    Existing status and exit contracts unchanged
    Stage receipts, parsers and probes unchanged
    No operations or approval changes
    Formatter not invoked; hint text only
  end note
end

note over P, C
  Each child requires fresh terminal approval
  before work begins on its stated scope.
  Acquisition consent covers host downloads,
  not guest network access or any subsequent
  provider calls.
end note
note over C, STATE
  Write stage intent before provider calls
  so ambiguous failures leave a bound
  attempt for review.
  Keep that state for reconciliation rather
  than automatic retry, reset or removal.
end note
note over C, VM
  Policy acceptance binds one attempt, name
  and digest before copying starts.
  It records consent, not proof that deny
  rules prevail over broader allows or grant
  reusable F9 authority.
end note
note over P, VM
  Accept diagnostic completion only for the
  matching STOP report, not F9 qualification.
  A host CLI timeout proves neither guest
  termination nor permission to start Cargo,
  KUnit or model work.
end note
@enduml
